…
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T5.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output 1:</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">[{"Metal_Source": [{"precursor_name": "AgNO3","amount": "0.2 mmol" }], …} ]
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T5.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input 2:</span> …
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A1.T5.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output 2:</span> …
<br class="ltx_break">…</span>
</span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Prompt template used for LLM entity extraction tasks, exemplified by CSD-MOFs dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix A ICL Prompt Template ‣ ALLabel: Three-stage Active Learning for LLM-based Entity Recognition using Demonstration Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we design an ICL prompt template for LLM entity extraction tasks, which consists of the following sections: &lt;Role Description, Task Description, Background Information, Format, Example&gt;. By adopting the prompt template, LLMs can leverage external knowledge to accurately understand the entities to be extracted.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Calculation Rules of Extraction Metrics</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Measurement Methods of Text Similarity</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use BM25 as the retriever to compute the similarity score between each test query and example in the main experiments. BM25 is a probabilistic information retrieval model that ranks documents based on the frequency of query terms within the documents. It balances term frequency (how often a term appears in a document) with inverse document frequency (how rare a term is across the entire document set), thus giving more weight to terms that are significant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The scoring function of BM25 between a paragraph with <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> terms and a document in a pool of length <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A2.E3.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:21.3pt;vertical-align:-12.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(30.6pt,-1.9pt) scale(1.21546424339905,1.21546424339905) ;">
<p id="A2.E3.2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.E3.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Score}(p,d)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{IDF}(p_{i})\cdot\frac{f(p_{i},d)\cdot(k_{1}+1)}{f(p_{i},d)+k_{1}\left(1-b+b\cdot\frac{|d|}{\text{avg\_dl}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Score</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mtext>IDF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mtext>avg_dl</mtext></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Score}(p,d)=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\text{IDF}(p_{i})\cdot\frac{f(p_{i},d)\cdot(k_{1}+1)}{f(p_{i},d)+k_{1}\left(1-b+b\cdot\frac{|d|}{\text{avg\_dl}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="0" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(p_{i},d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p_{i},d)</annotation></semantics></math> is the term frequency of <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in document <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|</annotation></semantics></math> is the length of document <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">avg_dl</span> is the average length of all documents in the demonstration pool, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{IDF}(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>IDF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{IDF}(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse document frequency of term <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> are hyperparameters of the model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the generalizability of ALLabel across different text similarity measurement methods, we also perform complementary experiment using Sentence-BERT as the retriever and observe consistent trends from Table <a href="#A2.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ B.1 Measurement Methods of Text Similarity ‣ Appendix B Calculation Rules of Extraction Metrics ‣ ALLabel: Three-stage Active Learning for LLM-based Entity Recognition using Demonstration Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, which suggests that ALLabel is robust to variations of similarity measurement methods. We observe that using Sentence-BERT as the retriever yields slightly lower performance compared to BM25, which is why we use BM25 as the retriever in the main experiments shown in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 Setup ‣ 5 Experiment ‣ ALLabel: Three-stage Active Learning for LLM-based Entity Recognition using Demonstration Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T6" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A2.T6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:37.2pt;vertical-align:-17.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-111.6pt,12.0pt) scale(0.6,0.6) ;">
<p id="A2.T6.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:568.2pt;height:61.2pt;vertical-align:-28.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">20</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">30</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">35</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">40</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">45</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">50</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">55</span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">60</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Random (SBERT)</span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="81.8_{1.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>81.8</mn><mn>1.1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">81.8_{1.1}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="A2.T6.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="83.3_{1.2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>83.3</mn><mn>1.2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">83.3_{1.2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
